Hi,

I'm new to NIMBLE and thought I'd try to code up a simple mixed model to get a feel for how NIMBLE works. I thought it'd be fun to use the data / modified model from Piepho & Ogutu (2002) <https://link.springer.com/article/10.1198/108571102366>, which can be fit using lmer from lme4 (so it seemed like a good place to start). However, I couldn't get the model to compile and there was a warning message issued when the nimbleModel function was called. A MWE is provided in the attached ZIP folder (I'm using a Windows 10 OS).

I'm probably doing something dumb, but can't spot it at the moment. I was hoping a fresh set of eyes could get me going in the right direction.

Thanks!

Josh

